/*!
\page page_sttofpidtraits StTofPidTraits

\brief Legacy STAR TOF patch particle identification traits for a matched track.

\section sttofpidtraits_overview Overview

\ref StTofPidTraits stores PID information for a track matched to a hit in the original
STAR TOF patch detector (operated during early runs, 2001–2004).  This was a small
scintillator-array detector covering a limited azimuthal sector at mid-rapidity,
the predecessor to the full BTOF barrel system.

The class stores the hit cell address (tray/module/cell), the measured TOF, path length,
velocity β, and nσ values for four species hypotheses (e, π, K, p).

\section sttofpidtraits_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code{.txt}
StObject
  └── StTrackPidTraits
           └── StTofPidTraits
\endcode

\section sttofpidtraits_members Data Members

| Member | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| \c mTray | \c Int_t | TOF tray number. |
| \c mModule | \c Int_t | Module number within the tray. |
| \c mCell | \c Int_t | Cell number within the module. |
| \c mTof | \c Float_t | Measured time of flight (ns). |
| \c mPathLength | \c Float_t | Path length from vertex to hit (cm). |
| \c mBeta | \c Float_t | β = v/c. |
| \c mSigmaElectron | \c Float_t | nσ from electron hypothesis; +999 if unset. |
| \c mSigmaPion | \c Float_t | nσ from pion hypothesis; +999 if unset. |
| \c mSigmaKaon | \c Float_t | nσ from kaon hypothesis; +999 if unset. |
| \c mSigmaProton | \c Float_t | nσ from proton hypothesis; +999 if unset. |

\section sttofpidtraits_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
const StTofPidTraits* tof = nullptr;
for (const StTrackPidTraits* p : track->pidTraits()) {
    tof = dynamic_cast<const StTofPidTraits*>(p);
    if (tof) break;
}

if (tof) {
    double measTof = tof->tof();          // ns
    double beta    = tof->beta();         // v/c
    double p       = track->geometry()->momentum().mag();
    double m2      = p*p*(1./(beta*beta) - 1.);  // (GeV/c²)²

    if (std::abs(tof->sigmaPion()) < 2.) { /* pion */ }
}
\endcode

\see StTrackPidTraits
\see StBTofPidTraits
\see StTofCollection
\see StTrack
*/
